      "text": "note: chunking (with example)\n\nexample:\n\noriginal file = abcdefgh\nfixed chunk size = 2 → [ab] [cd] [ef] [gh]\n\nnow insert d → abdcdefgh\n\nnew chunks → [ab] [dc] [de] [fg] [h...]\n\n👉 all chunks after change are shifted → hashes change →\nalmost full file re-upload\n\nBUT BUT BUT\n\nin real systems, we use content-defined chunking (not fixed\nsize). it is also called as rolling hash like Rabin fingerprint\n\nchunks are based on content, not position.\n\nso after change, only nearby chunk changes, rest remain\nsame.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "note: chunking (with example)\n\nexample:\n\noriginal file = abcdefgh\nfixed chunk size = 2 → [ab] [cd] [ef] [gh]\n\nnow insert d → abdcdefgh\n\nnew chunks → [ab] [dc] [de] [fg] [h...]\n\n👉 all chunks after change are shifted → hashes change → almost full file re-upload\n\nBUT BUT BUT\n\nin real systems, we use content-defined chunking (not fixed size). it is also called as rolling hash like Rabin fingerprint\n\nchunks are based on content, not position.\n\nso after change, only nearby chunk changes, rest remain same.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vDBSGcbjxnrpkoXCn3Vm3",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -1395.6542168336484,
      "y": 55248.47825800555,
      "width": 1216.1499997048181,
      "height": 1022.8057643148568,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "r2DxK_HCgIE90__xGZWzQ",
        "VB8INbESekRLb9sSObtEQ",
        "tLgKzq2TlKJWW869g6mIr"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNH",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1500894572,
      "version": 336,
      "versionNonce": 1926719877,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778475158638,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YIJNlWnO6oSFcAsnJGZz9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1355.8046416006025,
      "y": 55270.255563820014,
      "width": 1134.755615234375,
      "height": 990,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "r2DxK_HCgIE90__xGZWzQ",
        "VB8INbESekRLb9sSObtEQ",
        "tLgKzq2TlKJWW869g6mIr"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2027929172,
      "version": 1106,
      "versionNonce": 1473355083,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778475158638,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "validating checksum after every chunk upload is not a good idea.\n\nexample: if file size is 20GB and chunk size is 5MB, \nthen thousands of chunks will be uploaded.\n\nif file upload svc validates checksum for every chunk immediately, \nit becomes very busy and upload performance goes down.\n\nso better approach:\ndo not validate every chunk during upload.\nafter all chunks are uploaded, client sends final commit request.\nthen file upload svc triggers separate validator svc.\nvalidator svc validates all chunks asynchronously:\n    checks all chunks are present\n    compares expected checksum with storage checksum\n    marks file as valid/invalid\n\nonly after successful validation, file upload svc calls file metadata svc.\nthen metadata svc saves final file metadata in metadata DB.\nthis decouples upload and validation, so upload svc stays lightweight \nand system performs better.\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "validating checksum after every chunk upload is not a good idea.\n\nexample: if file size is 20GB and chunk size is 5MB, \nthen thousands of chunks will be uploaded.\n\nif file upload svc validates checksum for every chunk immediately, \nit becomes very busy and upload performance goes down.\n\nso better approach:\ndo not validate every chunk during upload.\nafter all chunks are uploaded, client sends final commit request.\nthen file upload svc triggers separate validator svc.\nvalidator svc validates all chunks asynchronously:\n    checks all chunks are present\n    compares expected checksum with storage checksum\n    marks file as valid/invalid\n\nonly after successful validation, file upload svc calls file metadata svc.\nthen metadata svc saves final file metadata in metadata DB.\nthis decouples upload and validation, so upload svc stays lightweight \nand system performs better.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "SDPnTXdKy-IO1aSesgqPZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1810.5919521151675,
      "y": 56407.17447229246,
      "width": 796.463623046875,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "tLgKzq2TlKJWW869g6mIr"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 362370924,
      "version": 160,
      "versionNonce": 2107240677,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778475158638,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "post-processing\n\nafter upload is completed and metadata is saved:\n\nfile metadata svc publishes event to Kafka.\n\npost-processing services consume this event.\n\nthey perform tasks like:\n\nthumbnail generation\nvirus scan\nindexing\n\nthis is async and does not block upload.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "post-processing\n\nafter upload is completed and metadata is saved:\n\nfile metadata svc publishes event to Kafka.\n\npost-processing services consume this event.\n\nthey perform tasks like:\n\nthumbnail generation\nvirus scan\nindexing\n\nthis is async and does not block upload.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5cMvcangBS6kHvpbaZ4r3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -773.8937192498533,
      "y": 56407.17447155837,
      "width": 1168.523681640625,
      "height": 1440,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "tLgKzq2TlKJWW869g6mIr"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1550498516,
      "version": 137,
      "versionNonce": 904248299,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778475158638,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "deduplication:\n\nwhen file upload is completed, system checks if same file already exists.\nthis is done using:\n    file hash / fingerprint\n\nif same file already exists:\n    no need to store file again in S3\n    metadata svc just creates new reference for that user\n    \nexample:\n    user A uploads file → stored in S3\n    user B uploads same file → no new upload\n    both users point to same file data\n    \nthis saves:\n    storage cost\n    bandwidth\n\n\n\n\nchunk-level deduplication (advanced):\n\ninstead of full file, system can also deduplicate at chunk level.\nif some chunks already exist in storage:\n    skip uploading those chunks\n    reuse existing chunks\n\nthis is useful when:\n    similar files\n    partial updates",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "deduplication:\n\nwhen file upload is completed, system checks if same file already exists.\nthis is done using:\n    file hash / fingerprint\n\nif same file already exists:\n    no need to store file again in S3\n    metadata svc just creates new reference for that user\n    \nexample:\n    user A uploads file → stored in S3\n    user B uploads same file → no new upload\n    both users point to same file data\n    \nthis saves:\n    storage cost\n    bandwidth\n\n\n\n\nchunk-level deduplication (advanced):\n\ninstead of full file, system can also deduplicate at chunk level.\nif some chunks already exist in storage:\n    skip uploading those chunks\n    reuse existing chunks\n\nthis is useful when:\n    similar files\n    partial updates",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZjD7L_5SULlDbP7O7zRMz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7915.314877791336,
      "y": 41519.21438233684,
      "width": 866.0877685546875,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1845116082,
      "version": 64,
      "versionNonce": 966515442,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778265804908,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "there are 2 types of users: viewer and content creator",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "there are 2 types of users: viewer and content creator",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "th6ji9B6DXRiHkyDnFP9e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8019.922200439218,
      "y": 43884.125244530806,
      "width": 666.8475341796875,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1867118446,
      "version": 232,
      "versionNonce": 1079754866,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778267277438,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "assume now like to transcode in multiple format like \n1080 + 720 + 480 + 360 + 240 + 144 \n\ntotal size = x + x/2 + x/4 + x/8 + x/16 + x/32  =  2x\n\navg size of 1 video in all format  = 600 mb",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "assume now like to transcode in multiple format like \n1080 + 720 + 480 + 360 + 240 + 144 \n\ntotal size = x + x/2 + x/4 + x/8 + x/16 + x/32  =  2x\n\navg size of 1 video in all format  = 600 mb",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c19XfYsJlCBNjFSQ7O8Hy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8685.94537128985,
      "y": 44583.388029785194,
      "width": 359.5477294921875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2110210286,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 573029102,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778268130100,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "always use either 1 or 3 or 5",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "always use either 1 or 3 or 5",
      "autoResize": true,
