    },
    {
      "id": "OZIZR6SoKX30zk5hwRUSC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8636.795407896061,
      "y": 45563.07582436942,
      "width": 1193.5830078125,
      "height": 1260,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1427570094,
      "version": 1657,
      "versionNonce": 526587758,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778269887243,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "creator uplaoding video can be of 1m or 10m or 2h\n\nso its not feasible to upload in one go. and also not possible to send entire video\nto server. so we will create chunks of videos.\n\nso instead we will create session for user first.. and cretor can use that session to \nupload video in chunks\n\n\nupload request:     POST    /v1/videos?uploadType=resumable\n\n            this will return session uri    =     /v1/videos?uploadType=resumable&sessionId=123\n\n\nwe are using resumable that means we are saying to server that we will beuploaidng \nchunk by chunk since video is too large\nso even if connection drops we can resume easily withou reuploading duplicate videose\n\nin this url we will be passing viddeo metadata like name size type format. and it will be stored \nand then return returned session url \n\ncontent cretor can use this sesion url to upload video chunks by chunks\n\n\nupload chunks:    PUT     /v1/videos/uploadType=resumable&sessionId=123\n\nin body we will pass chunks. with chunk number and binary format of the video\n\n\n\n\n\nwatch video;      GET       /v1/videos/watch/{videoId}              return manifest file.\n\nmanifest file contains location of all chunks.\nuser can use that manifest file to fetch video chunks from cdn using hls protocol",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "creator uplaoding video can be of 1m or 10m or 2h\n\nso its not feasible to upload in one go. and also not possible to send entire video\nto server. so we will create chunks of videos.\n\nso instead we will create session for user first.. and cretor can use that session to \nupload video in chunks\n\n\nupload request:     POST    /v1/videos?uploadType=resumable\n\n            this will return session uri    =     /v1/videos?uploadType=resumable&sessionId=123\n\n\nwe are using resumable that means we are saying to server that we will beuploaidng \nchunk by chunk since video is too large\nso even if connection drops we can resume easily withou reuploading duplicate videose\n\nin this url we will be passing viddeo metadata like name size type format. and it will be stored \nand then return returned session url \n\ncontent cretor can use this sesion url to upload video chunks by chunks\n\n\nupload chunks:    PUT     /v1/videos/uploadType=resumable&sessionId=123\n\nin body we will pass chunks. with chunk number and binary format of the video\n\n\n\n\n\nwatch video;      GET       /v1/videos/watch/{videoId}              return manifest file.\n\nmanifest file contains location of all chunks.\nuser can use that manifest file to fetch video chunks from cdn using hls protocol",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
